                <note rend="inline" type="source">No. 301.</note>
                <head>Mr. Davis to Mr.
                        Brent.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. <hi rendition="#small-caps">5.]</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi><hi
                                rendition="#italic"> Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1870-11-01"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >November</hi> 1, 1870.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Your dispatch, No. 238, of the 27th ultimo,
                    accompanied by further correspondence in regard to the appointment of Colonel
                    Farrand as bearer of dispatches, has been received. The arguments of the
                    Peruvian minister for foreign affairs against the legality of that appointment
                    appear to have been answered by anticipation in the instruction to you, No. 3,
                    of the 19th ultimo.</p>
            </div>
